  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>spiramycin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J01FA02</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>one compartment, IV dosing <small>(PK_1C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Elazab ST et al. 2021</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>chickens</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>spiramycin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_spiramycin/Spiramycin_Elazab2021_oral\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>Cmax (µg/mL)</td><td>4.78</td><td>µg/mL</td><td><small>Cmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>Tmax (h)</td><td>2.00</td><td>h</td><td><small>tmax</small></td></tr><tr><td>λz (1/h)</td><td>0.12</td><td>1/h</td><td><small>kel</small></td></tr><tr><td>T1/2 λz (h)</td><td>6.25</td><td>h</td><td><small>t1/2z</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUC0-last (µg*h/mL)</td><td>23.11</td><td>µg*h/mL</td><td><small>AUClast</small></td></tr><tr><td>AUC0-∞ (µg*h/mL)</td><td>23.61</td><td>µg*h/mL</td><td><small>AUC∞</small></td></tr><tr><td>Vz_F_obs (L/kg)</td><td>6.58</td><td>L/kg</td><td><small>V</small></td></tr><tr><td>MRT (h)</td><td>6.63</td><td>h</td><td><small>MRT</small></td></tr><tr><td>F (%)</td><td>77.18</td><td></td><td><small>Fab</small></td></tr></table><h4>About spiramycin</h4><p>Spiramycin is a macrolide antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections and has also been used as a coccidiostat. It remains an approved antibacterial for systemic use, available alone and in combination with other antibiotics, though it has been withdrawn in some markets.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q422265\">Wikidata Q422265</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p